  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q36-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Show that $\\tan75^\\circ+\\cot75^\\circ=4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4$.\n\nExpand $\\tan(30^\\circ+45^\\circ)=2+\\sqrt3$ and use $\\cot75^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan75^\\circ&=\\frac{\\tan30^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}{1-\\tan30^\\circ\\tan45^\\circ}\\\\\\tan75^\\circ&=\\frac{\\frac1{\\sqrt3}+1}{1-\\frac1{\\sqrt3}}\\\\\\tan75^\\circ&=\\frac{(1+\\sqrt3)(\\sqrt3+1)}{(\\sqrt3-1)(\\sqrt3+1)}\\\\\\tan75^\\circ&=\\frac{4+2\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\tan75^\\circ&=2+\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot75^\\circ&=\\frac1{2+\\sqrt3}\\\\\\cot75^\\circ&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{(2+\\sqrt3)(2-\\sqrt3)}\\\\\\cot75^\\circ&=2-\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan75^\\circ+\\cot75^\\circ&=(2+\\sqrt3)+(2-\\sqrt3)\\\\\\tan75^\\circ+\\cot75^\\circ&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
